<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47560" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Taurīni</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Northern Italy</i>, <i>near the
				modern Turin</i> (Augusta Taurinorum), <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 17,
				21, § 123</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21,
				38 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 66</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Taurīnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the Taurini</i>, <i>Taurine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 646</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
